The existing research studies focus on evaluating Large Language Models, monitoring their performance and analyzing execution traces to identify errors. 
These studies highlight the importance of tracking response quality, latency, token usage and system reliability in AI applications. 
They also show that proper monitoring helps developers understand and improve LLM performance. 
Based on these findings, our project aims to develop an LLM Observability Dashboard using Langfuse Tracing to bring important monitoring 
information together in a single, easy-to-use interface, helping developers analyze performance, manage costs and identify errors efficiently.
